IMPLEMENTATION FAMILY

derived from:
structural region / provenance.

DEPENDENCY FINGERPRINT

four synthetic binary dependency axes.

CONTEXT-RESPONSE TRAITS

three low-dimensional latent response coordinates.

The fourth dependency axis is intentionally:
NEVER FAILED
in the historical disturbance distribution.

It becomes:
an unpredicted future shock.

KNOWN DISTURBANCE SET
Six disturbance classes:

compute scarcity;

memory scarcity;

bandwidth scarcity;

canonical-family failure;

dependency-0 failure;

future context shift along a known response axis.

A learned expected-value controller knows:
the historical frequencies
of these disturbance classes.

RARE / UNPREDICTED TEST SET
Four shocks:

dependency-3 failure
not seen historically;

new context shift along a different response direction;

different implementation-family failure;

compound:
dependency + bandwidth shock.

RETENTION BUDGETS
Tested portfolio sizes:

K = 4
6
8.

The canonical implementation is retained.

Remaining slots contain:
cryptic variants.

POLICIES

RANDOM RETENTION

RESOURCE-DIVERSITY
farthest-point retention using only:
compute/memory/bandwidth vectors.

MULTI-AXIS NOVELTY
farthest-point retention over a mixed structural feature vector containing:

resource metabolism
+
family provenance
+
dependency fingerprint
+
context traits.

EXPECTED FUTURE VALUE
greedily add the implementation that maximizes:
expected best available function
under:
the KNOWN historical disturbance distribution.

HYBRID
combine:

marginal expected future value

+
bounded multi-axis novelty.

This intentionally reserves:
some option value
for:
unknown unknowns.

