PRIMARY EXPECTED-VALUE FAILURE
The learned-disturbance portfolio is:
excellent
on exactly the shocks it was optimized for.

But:
all retained variants accidentally share
the unseen dependency-3 vulnerability.

The new dependency failure produces:
TOTAL FUNCTION LOSS.

Thus:

EXPECTED FUTURE VALUE
UNDER THE LEARNED DISTRIBUTION

IS NOT
THE SAME AS:

FUTURE REACHABILITY.

This is an unknown-unknown failure.

