but to:
keeping several nearby futures reachable.

This is:
evolvability as a resource-allocation problem.

GENERAL PRINCIPLE
DO NOT OPTIMIZE
ONLY FOR:

EXPECTED FUTURE.

AND DO NOT OPTIMIZE
ONLY FOR:

ABSTRACT DIVERSITY.

Retain a bounded portfolio balancing:

LEARNED EXPECTED VALUE

+

STRUCTURAL / FAILURE-MODE NOVELTY

+

PERMANENT MEMORY COST.

DECISION
AR-H86 is POSITIVE WITH AN UNKNOWN-SHOCK LIMIT FOR PURE EXPECTED-VALUE RETENTION.

Supported synthetically:

- historical expected-value optimization can overfit the observed disturbance distribution;
- a portfolio can be highly optimized yet catastrophically share an unseen vulnerability;
- multi-axis structural novelty improves rare-shock reachability;
- a hybrid expected-value + novelty policy strongly improves worst-case function with small known-regime cost;
- six variants outperform four in future reachability at the tested geometry;
- eight provide little further benefit;
- option value has diminishing returns.

Not demonstrated:

- learned representation of failure axes;
- real shock probabilities;
- online portfolio replacement;
- correlated canary error;
- inheritance of option portfolios;
- relationship between future reachability and actual intelligence.

NEXT HIGH-VALUE MOVE
AR-H87 — ENDOGENOUS EXPLORATION BUDGET / WHEN TO GENERATE CRYPTIC VARIANTS

H85-H86 assume:
neutral variants are available to choose from.

But exploration itself costs:
compute,
testing,
and
memory bandwidth.

Question:

WHEN SHOULD THE ORGANISM SPEND RESOURCE
TO GENERATE NEW FUNCTION-PRESERVING VARIANTS?

Candidate drivers:

- current portfolio fragility;
- low option coverage;
- environmental volatility;
- resource surplus;
- long stable periods;
- impending disturbance prediction;
- exploration cost.

Compare:

A.
constant neutral exploration;

B.
explore only under spare capacity;

C.
option-gap-driven exploration;

D.
stress-triggered exploration;

E.
exploration during crisis;

F.
false volatility causing unnecessary diversification.

Desired:

stable resource surplus
may fund:
cryptic variation.

acute emergency
should not:
consume scarce repair capacity
on speculative evolvability.

This would make:
EVOLVABILITY ITSELF
a dynamically budgeted metabolic process.

Do not execute STAB-18-R1 during this lane.

